hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15946","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama al-Laythi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Alqama, from Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may utter a word from the pleasure of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, not thinking it reaches what it reached, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic writes for him by it His pleasure until the Day of Resurrection. And a man may utter a word from the wrath of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, not thinking it reaches what it reached, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic writes upon him by it His wrath until the Day of Resurrection. He said: So Alqama used to say: How much speech has the hadith of Bilal ibn al-Harith prevented me from."
"15947","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, he said, Ibn Rabi'a ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman informed me, from al-Harith ibn Bilal, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is the annulment of Hajj for us specifically or for people generally? He said: Rather, for us specifically."
"15948","Quraysh ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, he said, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said, Rabi'a ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman informed me, he said: I heard al-Harith ibn Bilal ibn al-Harith narrating from his father, he said: O Messenger of Allah, do you see the tamattu' of Hajj, is it for us specifically or for people generally? So he said: No, rather for us specifically."
